# standard.async — EAV-native binding to the libuv event-loop async runtime.
#
# This is the *libuv* concurrency model — a single-threaded event loop, NOT OS
# threads. There is NO async knowledge in the compiler: each operation is a
# `body runtimeBinding <symbol>` over the eav_async_* C ABI (runtime/eav_async.c,
# a thin shim on SemanticScript/runtime/native_async built with
# SEM_ASYNC_WITH_LIBUV against third_party/libuv). The compiler lowers each op to
# an extern call to that symbol; this module owns the typed contract
# (README ss11/ss26/ss34), exactly as standard.sqlite does for the SQLite engine.
#
# An AsyncFuture is OpaquePointer (a handle scheduled on the process-wide loop);
# on x86-64 the pointer and an i64 share the ABI register, so the lowering is
# exact. A future is created and armed by `delay`; nothing runs until the loop is
# driven by `await` (which blocks the calling fiber, cooperatively, until ready)
# or `runOnce` (which turns the loop one step without blocking).

standardAsync is module
standardAsync path standard.async
standardAsync exports delay
standardAsync exports await
standardAsync exports runOnce
standardAsync exports withTimeout
standardAsync exports awaitResult
standardAsync exports cancel
standardAsync purpose "Typed EAV contract over the libuv event-loop async runtime via the eav_async_* ABI"
standardAsync invariant "Every operation is a runtimeBinding to an eav_async_* symbol; no async logic lives in the compiler"

AsyncFuture is alias
AsyncFuture for OpaquePointer
AsyncFuture purpose "An opaque future handle armed on the libuv loop, resolved by await"

AsyncMillis is alias
AsyncMillis for Int64
AsyncMillis purpose "A non-negative delay in milliseconds, scheduled as a libuv timer"

delay is operation
delay in delayMs AsyncMillis
delay in value Int64
delay out AsyncFuture
delay async yes
delay body runtimeBinding eav_async_delay_start
delay purpose "Arm a future that completes with `value` after `delayMs` on the event loop"
delay invariant "Returns immediately; the timer fires only once the loop is driven by await/runOnce"
delay suppress SS5000 because "runtimeBinding seam to the eav_async_* libuv runtime; the typed home is this module"

await is operation
await in future AsyncFuture
await out Int64
await async yes
await body runtimeBinding eav_async_await
await purpose "Drive the event loop until the future is ready, then return its resolved value"
await invariant "Cooperatively runs the loop; the value is the one the timer callback completed the future with"
await suppress SS5000 because "runtimeBinding seam to the eav_async_* libuv runtime; the typed home is this module"

runOnce is operation
runOnce out Int32
runOnce body runtimeBinding eav_async_run_once
runOnce purpose "Run one turn of the event loop without blocking (cooperative progress / poll)"
runOnce suppress SS5000 because "runtimeBinding seam to the eav_async_* libuv runtime; the typed home is this module"

withTimeout is operation
withTimeout in delayMs AsyncMillis
withTimeout in value Int64
withTimeout in timeoutMs AsyncMillis
withTimeout out AsyncFuture
withTimeout async yes
withTimeout body runtimeBinding eav_async_timeout_start
withTimeout purpose "Arm a future like delay, but resolved as timed-out if timeoutMs elapses first"
withTimeout invariant "A second libuv timer races the value timer; whichever fires first wins"
withTimeout suppress SS5000 because "runtimeBinding seam to the eav_async_* libuv runtime; the typed home is this module"

awaitResult is operation
awaitResult in future AsyncFuture
awaitResult out Int64
awaitResult async yes
awaitResult body runtimeBinding eav_async_await_result
awaitResult outParam
awaitResult purpose "Drive the loop until ready; bind the value and surface timeout/cancel as a fallible error"
awaitResult invariant "Returns the value with ok status, or a non-zero status (timeout/cancelled) as the call's error"
awaitResult suppress SS5000 because "runtimeBinding seam to the eav_async_* libuv runtime; the typed home is this module"

cancel is operation
cancel in future AsyncFuture
cancel out Int32
cancel body runtimeBinding eav_async_cancel
cancel purpose "Cancel a not-yet-ready future; a later awaitResult resolves it as cancelled"
cancel suppress SS5000 because "runtimeBinding seam to the eav_async_* libuv runtime; the typed home is this module"
